  Write an equation to represent this problem.  Jen pays $400 for supplies.  The cost of the supplies and the cost of the travel is $600 in total.  The equation is 0.5x + 400 = 600.  The cost of the travel is $200.
\end{blockquote}

The answer key is 0.5x + 400 = 600, but I can't seem to figure out how to solve it.
